\title{listsr: Find Pattern in the Lists You Already Collect}
\description{
A small toolkit for turning the ragged, everyday lists people already keep (sites, and the items found at each) into reproducible groups. It reads ragged list text into a binary two-way table, scans frequencies, measures Jaccard dissimilarity, draws dendrograms (optionally coloured by external metadata), and cuts a tree into groups by the "most variable site sets the line" assessment-line rule. It is the companion engine to the 'lists' document and shares lineage with the 'coenosr' package, which reads Braun-Blanquet releve files.
